Subject: [PATCH] round C1.4: new accounts land on the validated next, not "/"

Round T3 (relay 6f8241a): both new accounts (c2e2e, c2admin) finished
their first sign-in on the sign-up branch of the combined Clerk card and
landed on "/" instead of `next`; existing accounts honoured `next`.
With zero legacy users every production user takes this path.

The card is <SignIn withSignUp>. forceRedirectUrl / fallbackRedirectUrl only
govern the sign-in branch; the sign-up branch reads
signUpForceRedirectUrl / signUpFallbackRedirectUrl, which were unset, so
Clerk fell back to "/". Set both to the same `next` that safeNextTarget()
already validated. No other change; the middleware marker check, the switch
check and the next validation are untouched.

File owner note: app/goaa-clerk-login/page.tsx is in Aika's area; this is a
two-prop addition for her review.

Test: scripts/test-clerk-signup-redirect.cjs (2); c2-clerk
test-candidate-shape still 8/8 locally.

